  {
   "text": "I built the hex cup as an 80 mm across-corners hexagon, 100 mm tall, with 2 mm walls and a 2 mm floor. The honeycomb cuts did not go through. The tool reported \"holes not cut\" on all 21 holes in each attempt, so the walls are solid right now.\n\nI made three versions while trying to place the holes, so the project has three objects. The first two (\"Hex pen cup\" and \"Hex pen cup honeycomb\") have no holes. The third, \"Hex pen cup honeycomb v3\", has the same body and the intended hole layout, but it is not cut either. Please delete the first two in Model.\n\nThe honeycomb is also not a true hex pattern. The tools can only cut round holes along the X, Y or Z axis. The two flat walls facing front and back are the only ones a straight hole can reach, and the four angled walls would need a different cut. Your options:\n\n1. Cut the honeycomb by hand in Model. Hexagonal through-cuts on all six walls are a boolean subtract, which takes a few minutes.\n2. Accept round holes on the two front and back flats only, about 21 holes in a staggered grid. I would need to find a way to make the holes cut, which I have not managed yet.\n\nNothing has been sliced or sent to the printer. Which do you want?"
